From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] eglut: avoid blocking on shared Wayland display fd

NVIDIA EGL dispatches buffer-release events from a private queue and may
consume display-fd readiness before eglut handles it. Poll periodically and
drain only pending events so eglut cannot block after a readiness race.
---
 src/egl/eglut/eglut_wayland.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/egl/eglut/eglut_wayland.c b/src/egl/eglut/eglut_wayland.c
--- a/src/egl/eglut/eglut_wayland.c
+++ b/src/egl/eglut/eglut_wayland.c
@@ -523,3 +523,3 @@ _eglutNativeEventLoop(void)
       unsigned poll_count = 2 + (display.seat.rate > 0);
-      if (poll(pollfds, poll_count, -1) == -1)
+      if (poll(pollfds, poll_count, 16) == -1)
          break;
@@ -537,3 +537,3 @@ _eglutNativeEventLoop(void)
       if (pollfds[0].revents & POLLIN) {
-         ret = wl_display_dispatch(display.display);
+         ret = wl_display_dispatch_pending(display.display);
          if (ret == -1)
